        "conviction_level": "medium",
        "overnight_surprise": true
      },
      {
        "title": "Grains drift on harvest",
        "body": "- Dec corn is at **$4.51¼** overnight, half a cent under Wednesday's $4.51¾ settle.\n- November beans are at $12.16¾, down 7¾ cents, after three straight lower closes.\n- Feedstuffs said soybeans and winter wheat faded lower Wednesday, with corn the only grain to hold up.",
        "so_what": "Beans keep sliding while corn holds its ground.",
        "conviction_level": "low",
        "overnight_surprise": false
      },
      {
        "title": "Crude eases on Iran talk",
        "body": "- WTI is at **$101.21** overnight, down 1.5%. Oilprice reports Vice President Vance contacted Iran's security council to restart peace talks. Supply fears from the Iran conflict have kept crude above $100 for months.\n- Natural gas is at $3.04, up 8.0%, as Oilprice reports record U.S. production.",
        "so_what": "Crude is still pricing in Iran supply risk, and diesel follows it.",
